==Feedback Update - Thursday, July 11th==
Before we kick things off: '''we are postponing today's planned Q&A for While Guthix Sleeps'''.

At this stage, we don't feel comfortable hosting a Q&A that gives confident answers to many of the questions we've seen from you. We'd like to protect our team's time to allow them to make necessary fixes and changes as soon as possible, while also further considering feedback on complicated topics like loot tables rather than overcorrecting with a knee-jerk reaction only a day after release. There's loads for us to get through and it's important for us to talk about things properly within the team before sharing our response with you all.

While we've got your attention, it makes sense to at least share where we're at so that you're not left totally in the dark without a Sapphire Lantern to guide you.

===Loot Tables===
As we have with most releases of late, we opted for a more cautious loot table than an overly generous one - this has worked well for us (and the health of the game) and is something we'll continue to do. That being said, we hear you loud and clear - the Tormented Demon loot tables need some work. We'll be taking the time to get this right and making sure that we're making a decision that's well-informed by data as well as your feedback. We'll be looking to speak in more detail on these next week when we have more datapoints for factors like kills per hour and/or unique prices. It's also worth pointing out that some of the intricacies of the demons' Shield mechanics and ways to really maximise your damage output and kills per hour don't seem to be particularly widespread - we're especially interested to see how the unique rates stack up as people get more efficient with their kills or start taking on multiple Tormented Demons at once.

Admittedly this doesn't tell you all that much, but to be crystal clear: we '''will''' be looking carefully at loot tables and plan to make changes in line with your feedback once we're armed with better data. We're ''always'' open to making changes where necessary, and is no exception.

While we're here though, a request! Please stop targeting or singling out individual developers while providing your feedback. In many cases, the developers being targeted aren't heavily involved with the content that you're criticising. In '''all''' cases, loot mechanics and tables are passed around the team and reviewed - we succeed as a team and we fail as a team. We're more than happy for you to be critical of our work as a team, but the repeated targeting of individual team members needs to stop.

===Hotfixes===
There are a couple of changes we can hotfix today, our devs are working away right now!

* We'll be doing a balance pass on the quest's combat difficulty compared to other Grandmaster quests. Effectively we just want to make sure that While Guthix Sleeps stacks up sensibly against the likes of Dragon Slayer 2 or Monkey Madness 2 after seeing feedback that it might feel a little too easy at the moment. If we do make changes here we likely won't go overboard, just enough to improve the challenge a little so that it better stands the test of time!
* Allow players to use temporary boosts for the crafting requirements of new unique items.

===Next Week===
If you scroll a little further down this post you'll see a table detailing a number of fixes we were able to make throughout yesterday, so it might be worth checking if any problems you encountered during the release have since been fixed.

We've also got a very clear sense of what we'd like to get into next week's game update:
* Renaming the Bone Claws to Burning Claws.
* Adding a teleport item to quickly take you to the Guthixian Temple, this will likely be a drop from Tormented Demons. The aim here is to cut down the time required running back either between trips or to collect loot from your gravestone. This should prove a nice additional reward since the added benefit is an increase in your kills per hour by significantly reducing your time between trips!
* Adding a UI icon when inside the Guthixian Temple that shows you how many demons you can tackle at once. This should address some of the confusion that many of you are facing where you're getting attacked by more demons than you intended, or haven't been able to find the right areas to tackle your Combat Achievements.

===Beyond Next Week===
This section loosely falls into two categories. The first is "simple fixes we'll be able to make but lower priority than those already listed" which is a bit of a mouthful. The second is "stuff we can't firmly commit to changing yet because we need more time to talk through it as a team".

Let's tackle the simple fixes first!
* Allow players to store the Broav inside their POH. We're not going to make this adorable little critter a fully-fledged pet, but you'll be able to keep your very own Broav at home - make sure to check in on him from time-to-time, or he'll track you down and steal all of your loot.
* Allow players to use temporary boosts for the crafting requirements of new unique items.
* Allow players to use runes from the Rune Pouch for Lucien's teleorb. Spoiler: he's got a teleorb, whatever that means...
* Allow players to store the Dark Squall Robes and Elite Black Armour in their POH Costume room. FashionScape is important, this feels like a no-brainer.
* Allow players to use the Emberlight for the Treasure Trail step requiring an Arclight in the Catacombs of Kourend.

While it's important to be clear: we are not able to hard-commit to any of these next points, we think it's equally important to give you a look at some of the conversations beyond loot tables that we'll be having in the near future.
* Talking through feedback on Lucien's new look and animations. This one's been hotly debated following a handful of you suggesting his new look could stand to be a little more fearsome.
* Talking through feedback on Laidee Gnonock's model. If you're not sure who this NPC is then we'll keep our mouths shut. Needless to say we'll be taking a look!
* Review changes we could make to the fight with the Dark Squall (whose actual name we're not using for spoiler purposes) to improve its accessibility for colourblind players.
* Consider restoring some of the missing text from Movario's notes about Dragonkin and Tormented Demons, so long as it lines up with our plans for Old School's narrative.
* Similarly, reviewing the dialogue that was ''removed'' from the original version of the quest and re-instating or adjusting where needed. Just like the above point, these inclusions need to line up with our plans for the likes of the Mahjarrat, the Stone of Jas and the Dragonkin, so we need to review carefully to strike up the right balance between more of the dialogue you were expecting and having it all make sense in Old School.
** On this one in particular, if you have some ideas about which bits of dialogue you'd like restoring then we'd love to hear from you. Let us know!

We're sure there's likely even more to come - it's only been a day after all - but for now this is more or less where we're at with everything.

Once more we'd like to apologise for postponing today's stream to last minute, it was a tough call for us to make but ultimately we want to spend our time where it's most effective right now and that's going to mean making fixes, talking through balancing changes and keeping an eye out for anything else we need to change.

Thank you so much to all of you who've played through While Guthix Sleeps already, please keep your feedback coming whether it's positive or negative, we really appreciate everything you've shared with us so far!

