==While Guthix Sleeps==
This week we're bringing one of RuneScape’s most iconic quests to Old School. It’s While Guthix Sleeps! The incredibly talented OnlyTrails has summed up our latest quest additions in video format for those who might want something to watch during downtime:

<center>{{Youtube|qmHw2nXBqtM}}</center>
<center>''If you can't see the video above, click ''[https://youtu.be/qmHw2nXBqtM?si=5YPngevw5Zro4UPZ here]'' to watch it!''</center>

This Grandmaster quest sees you continue the Mahjarrat storyline, hunting down one of the most powerful artefacts in existence while ensuring it doesn't fall into the wrong hands. 

This artefact is known by many names – most recently, the Stone of Jas. It has shaped the course of Gielinor’s history, from the creation of the first Runes to the fall of Zaros. It was last seen at the devastating end of the God Wars, when Zamorak, in a fit of rage, used it to reduce the land of Forinthry to the Wilderness we know today.

Angered by Zamorak’s actions, Guthix rose from his age-long slumber and banished the gods. He hid the Stone of Jas far underground, where it could never disturb the balance again...

But while Guthix sleeps, nefarious forces have been gathering; the Mahjarrat. Shaped by war and deadly ritual, their plans for the Stone can only lead to catastrophe.

Facing off against the Mahjarrat is nothing new for dedicated adventurers – at every turn, they seem to grow in power and wage war against the people of Gielinor. In their last attempt, we saw them set out to tear Varrock apart with an undead army in Defender of Varrock. What are they plotting now? You’ll have to play the quest to find out!

If all that lore is a bit much to digest, PoisonedPotion has condensed it all into one epic video breakdown. Check it out below:

<center>{{Youtube|4SQb6lH29x4}}</center>
<center>''If you can't see the video above, click ''[https://youtu.be/4SQb6lH29x4?si=H-ex4tFlFGUpFUaG here ]''to watch it!''</center>

==Requirements==
===Quest Requirements===
This grandmaster quest is not for the unprepared! You’ll need to complete the following quests before taking it on:

* Defender of Varrock
* The Path of Glouphrie
* Fight Arena
* Dream Mentor
* The Hand in the Sand
* Wanted
* Temple of the Eye
* Tears of Guthix
* Nature Spirit
* A Tail of Two Cats

You’ll also need a total of 180 Quest Points to start the quest.

===Skill Requirements===
Here are the skills you need to stand a chance against the evil Mahjarrat:

* 72 Thieving
* 67 Magic
* 66 Agility
* 65 Farming
* 65 Herblore
* 62 Hunter
* Ability to enter the Warriors' Guild

==Quest Rewards==

* 5 Quest Points
* 80,000 Thieving XP
* 75,000 Farming XP
* 75,000 Herblore XP
* 50,000 Hunter XP
* Access to the Ancient Guthixian Temple and tormented demons

If you think you’re ready to get started, head to Taverley and speak to Ivy Sophista, who’s keen to follow up on an ominous letter...

[[File:While Guthix Sleeps (1).png|600px|center]]


[[File:While Guthix Sleeps (2).png|thumb|600px|center|''If you need a visual, here's where you can start the quest!'']]

===Tormented Demons===
As part of this historic quest, we're summoning back an iconic enemy: the tormented demons. Wreathed in flame and called forth to stop you meddling in Mahjarrat plans, these monsters aren't to be taken lightly. But with great risk comes great reward, as the tormented demons have the chance to drop the Tormented Synapse and the brand-new Bone Claws.

The Tormented Synapse is a tradeable unique drop that can be used to craft three new Demonbane weapons: Emberlight, the Scorching Bow, and the Purging Staff. You’ll need at least level 74 in the relevant skill to craft all three weapons. Unlike other craftables, we’re not giving you the option to have a skilled NPC craft it for you. This means that mains and Irons alike will have to graft for their spoils, but these powerful weapons are well worth the effort.

We developed all four new weapons, including the Bone Claws, through community consultation, taking on your feedback and tweaking the stats so each item felt more in-line with their positioning. 

===Demonbane Weapons===
We discussed all the new weapons in detail in our [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/while-guthix-sleeps---rewards?oldschool=1 rewards blog], but there have been a few tweaks since then. Let’s get up to speed...

[[File:While Guthix Sleeps (3).png|400px|center]]


[[File:While Guthix Sleeps (4).png|400px|center]]


[[File:While Guthix Sleeps (5).png|400px|center]]

Emberlight is created from a fully charged Arclight and a Tormented Synapse, and you'll need 74 Smithing to do it. You no longer need to charge this weapon with Ancient Shards. It has increased Stab and Slash Accuracy, as well as the same 70% increased Accuracy and Damage bonuses as its predecessor. Additionally, it improves on Arclight’s Special Attack, lowering the Strength, Attack and Defence of demons by 15% of their base level +1, and non-demons by 5% of their base level +1. That’s a 5% increase!

Scorching Bow requires 74 Fletching and a Tormented Synapse, but once created has 124 Ranged Accuracy and 40 Ranged Strength. It also has 30% increased Accuracy and Damage against demons, plus a nasty Special Attack which binds your enemy for 5 ticks while dealing 1 bonus damage – and if they’re a demon, it binds them for 20 ticks, increasing the bonus damage to 5.

Purging Staff can be synthesised using a Tormented Synapse and 74 Crafting. Rather than giving you an outright damage boost against demons, this weapon instead autocasts combat spells from the Arceuus Spellbook. On its own that doesn’t sound like such a great reward – but using Demonbane spells will double the bonuses. Additionally, the Purging Staff has a Special Attack. You must be on the Arceuus Spellbook to cast it (which is handy, given the Staff’s effect), and you must be targeting a demon. When used, the Special Attack will cast the highest available Demonbane spell at your target. If your target is killed by the spell, you’ll restore 25% of your Special Attack energy, and the delay on your next attack will be reduced by 3.

If the sight of all those numbers fills you with DEMONIC RAGE, you’re ready to pick up our next weapon...

===Bone Claws===
[[File:While Guthix Sleeps (6).png|400px|center]]
As the Dragon Claws are remaining in Chambers of Xeric, we wanted to develop a new set of claws that matched the rush of landing the originals. The Bone Claws also bridge the gap in Melee spec weapons between the cheap and cheerful Dragon Dagger and the monstrously expensive Dragon Claws. You'll find that the Tormented Demons drop the singular Bone Claw, and you'll need to collect and combine two to get your hands on the finished Bone Claws.

This weapon works much the same as the latter, while giving you a chance to inflict Burn on your target. While Burnt, the target will be dealt 10 damage over the course of 40 ticks (1 every 4 ticks). This effect can stack up to five times.

So that's two new unique drops leading to four brand new demonic weapons – not a bad haul!

